Amazon-10590848.description:
Are you passionate about driving international business growth through innovative, AI-powered solutions? Join our TBAM+ team within Amazon Global Selling, where you'll manage a portfolio of China-based sellers as they scale their presence in Amazon's Australia marketplace. The TBAM+ team is a dedicated group of Account Managers focused on CN2AU medium and small sellers, combining strategic account management and incubation with scaled, data-driven operations. This role sits at the intersection of cross-border e-commerce, data analytics, and relationship management — helping sellers unlock new growth opportunities while delivering exceptional customer experiences.
As an Account Manager II on the TBAM+ team, you will own a large portfolio of CN2AU sellers, serving as their trusted advisor in the Australia marketplace. This is a one-to-many (portfolio) management role: you'll prioritize across a book of sellers, segment them by potential, and scale your impact by combining strategic engagement for key accounts with efficient, standardized playbooks and AI tools for the broader portfolio. You'll combine strategic thinking with hands-on execution, using data-driven insights to guide sellers from onboarding through scaling — making a measurable impact on international seller success.
Key job responsibilities
Manage a large portfolio of CN2AU sellers in the Australia marketplace, balancing engagement for key potential accounts with scaled, standardized playbooks for the broader book of business — coaching China-based sellers to maximize their marketplace presence;
Leverage AI tools and internal analytics platforms to analyze seller performance data, sales trends, and marketplace metrics at scale, turning insights into actionable recommendations that drive selection growth, feature adoption, and profitability across your portfolio;
Partner with sellers to achieve data quality standards and performance benchmarks, ensuring optimal product listings and customer experiences through expert use of internal tools and AI-powered solutions;
Identify common pain points across your seller base (compliance, logistics/FBA, selection, promotions, brand building) and collaborate with marketing teams and cross-functional stakeholders to resolve issues, implement best practices, and continuously improve seller support at scale
About the team
We are the TBAM+ team within Amazon Global Selling, enabling China-based sellers to thrive in Amazon's Australia marketplace. Each Account Manager owns a portfolio of CN2AU sellers, operating at the forefront of cross-border e-commerce where one-to-many account management meets AI and data tools to deliver results at scale. We foster a collaborative environment where continuous learning and innovation drive success. Our members grow their expertise in marketplace dynamics, scaled portfolio management, and data analysis — building the future of international e-commerce by empowering sellers with the insights, tools, and support they need to grow sustainably.

Amazon-10533681.description:
Amazon strives to be Earth's most customer-centric company where people can find and discover virtually anything they want to buy online. To serve the goal, Amazon has created one of the most advanced fulfillment and logistic networks in the world.
Amazon Global Logistics in China is a team of highly experienced logistics professionals, product & program manager and carrier specialists actively participating in Amazon's international expansion goals. We are seeking highly motivated individuals who are interested in improving the way products are bought, sold, and distributed on a global scale to join us in China.
Key job responsibilities
Key job responsibilities
Explores channels to connect with target new sellers who is interested in Amazon Global Logistics service;
Connects with sellers;
Help seller complete on-boarding process;
Help seller start to ship and grow their business;
Provided answers for Frequently Asked Questions on service introduction, on-boarding process etc.
A day in the life
A day in the life
Connect with sellers via e-mail, Wechat & phone calls;
Talk with sellers, provided answers for FAQ and guide seller go through on-boarding process;
Talk with seller, to solve their pain points during working with GM.
Wort out solution (from available GM product list ) to help seller reduce shipping cost, improving supply chain efficiency and win their trust.
Summarize seller portrait and improve Blurbs for target seller pitching.

Amazon-10529612.description:
Amazon has spent years building one of the world’s most efficient and optimized supply chains. Amazon Multi-Channel Commerce & Fulfillment (MCCF) solution is providing a third-party logistics and e-commerce solution that leverages Amazon's vast fulfillment network, technology and expertise to handle storage, picking, packing, shipping and after-sales of products ordered through diversified sales channels.
MCCF business is expanding rapidly in recently years, enabling sellers of all sizes to scale their logistics operations using Amazon’s leading fulfillment infrastructure and e-commerce frustracture. As a MCCF Senior Account Representative, you will support the expansion of MCCF business by identifying and onboarding the sellers across various verticals, driving adoption of MCCF among them by influencing onboarding, deepening partnerships, and collaborating cross-functionally to ensure a satisfactory seller experience.
Key job responsibilities
- Execute targeted outreach campaigns to acquire new sellers into the MCCF program, drive the growth of high potential sellers with incremental performance;
- Develop account-specific plans and drive execution through consultative and value selling;
- Conduct product pitches, engagement meetings, and follow-ups with prospective accounts;
- Track and report sales activities to Sales Leadership by using internal CRM and reporting tools;
- Build strong relationships with internal stakeholders across Product, Tech, Ops, and Marketing to ensure a seamless seller experience;
- Act as the voice of the customer to identify feature gaps and process improvements;
- Maintain a sensitivity on competitive offerings and industry trends, and enhance MCF market presence through attendance of industry influential conferences/events.

Amazon-10588420.requirements:
Basic qualifications
- Bachelor’s degree is required. MBA or advanced engineering degree is preferred;
- 5+ years in product management/product development/global sourcing/business development/project management is required;
- Experience in interacting with suppliers in different geographies are required;
- Self-motivated and results driven;
- High attention to detail, comfortable with “hands-on” management of tasks, and proven ability to manage multiple, competing priorities simultaneously;
- Demonstrated data-driven decision making and quantitative analysis skills;
- Proficient in Excel and SQL;
- Experience of managing large data set;
- Excellent English written and verbal communication skills.

Preferred qualifications
- Knowledge of Microsoft Excel (macros, pivots, lookups) at an advanced level
- Experience leading cross-functional teams to deliver projects on tight deadlines
- Experience building and analyzing cost/benefit scenarios and business cases and communicating results throughout the organization
- Experience in Tableau, QuickSight and Power BI are preferred.
